        "date": "2026-11-10T16:23:13Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app): an MCP move_model tool places and turns an imported part (#716)\n\nmove_model { name, position, rotation? } runs the GUI's MoveModel command\nthrough the document History, so a headless move is one undo step and every\nrefusal is the command's own text (a fixture, a work offset, the machine\ntable, an unknown name, a rotation that is not a quaternion). An omitted\nrotation keeps the part's current one. The reply lists the stock that moved\nwith the part (stock made from it, or a one-part document's stock), read\nfrom the new MoveModel::following_stock().\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/mcp_model.rs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
